.SH "نام (NAME)"
picom-inspect \- easily test your picom rules
.SH "خلاصه دستور (SYNOPSIS)"
.sp
\fBpicom\-inspect\fP [\fIOPTIONS\fP]
.SH "توضیحات (DESCRIPTION)"
.sp
\fBpicom\-inspect\fP matches your picom rules against a window of your choosing. It helps you test your rules, and shows you which ones of your rules (don\(cqt) work.
.SH "گزینه‌ها (OPTIONS)"
.sp
\fBpicom\-inspect\fP accepts all options that \fBpicom\fP does. Naturally, most of those options will not be relevant.
.sp
These are some of the options you might find useful (See \fBpicom\fP(1) for descriptions of what they do):
.sp
\fB\-\-config\fP, \fB\-\-log\-level\fP, \fB\-\-log\-file\fP, all the options related to rules.
.sp
\fBpicom\-inspect\fP also accepts some extra options:
.RS 4
.sp
\fB\-\-monitor\fP
.RS 4
Keep \fBpicom\-inspect\fP running in a loop, and dump information every time something changed about a window.
.RE
.RE
.SH "نکات (NOTES)"
.sp
\fBpicom\-inspect\fP is prototype right now. If you find any bug, for example, if rules are matched differently compared to \fBpicom\fP, please submit bug reports to:
.sp
.URL "https://github.com/yshui/picom" "" ""
